        /// <summary>
        /// Retrieves a selection of projection quality/accuracy parameters in use by the system.
        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// * **PartIntersectionToleranceMM**: When creating geometry from input points(from files), two points are considered the same if they are less than this distance apart (\&quot;heals\&quot; two different polygons together); how close a point is to a line before it is considered to intersect the line.   * **EnableCrosshairProjections:**:  When enabled (true) projection clients will overlay surface planar crosshairs over top of circular features (including holes). Configured by default in Virtek Server Manager &amp;gt; Iris Client &amp;gt; Projection Options \&quot;Project Crosshairs\&quot;; note this does not reflect whether or not crosshairs are actively being projected, as the Operator can enable/disable this in Iris Client &amp;gt; Options &amp;gt; \&quot;Project circle crosshairs\&quot;   * **DisplayCrosshairProjections:** When enabled (true) shows the location of crosshair projections in the Iris CAD model view; regardless of whether their (laser) projection is enabled by default (see EnableCrosshairProjections above) or is currently activated by Iris Client &amp;gt; Options &amp;gt; project circle crosshairs.   * BreakIntersectingPolygons -  Internal use only  * **CrosshairRadiusFitToleranceMillimeters** - how far from \&quot;circular\&quot; a circle point can be before it is no longer considered a circle (for crosshair purposes)  * **CrosshairCoplanarDeviationAngleTolerance** - how flat points on a circle have to be before it is no longer considered a circle (for crosshair purposes)  * **CrosshairMinimumNumberOfPointsInCircle** - a circle (for crosshair purposes) has to have at least this many points  * **ImageErrorTolerance** - the fundamental accuracy parameter; the laser is guaranteed to never sweep further away than this from nominal; lower values will result in slower laser sweeps and higher flicker  * **TextErrorTolerance** - same as above but for Projected Text; lower values &#x3D; sharper text characters but with more flicker  * **FocusToleranceFactor** - how accurate Focus Of Attention projections are vs. normal, specified as an ImageErrorTolerance multiplier - e.g. 10x more accurate, specify 0.1 for this parameter  * **ObjectFocus** - when true, Focus of Attention reduces focus to polygons, entities overlapping the retro; when false, Focus of Attention is a circular radius around the retro hit  * **FocusCheckPeriodMilliseconds** - Focus of Attention - how frequently FoA checks for persistence of the retro material  * **FocusTrackPeriodMilliseconds** - Laser octagon cursor - how frequently the laser octagon tracking checks for retro presence  * IsFoaDetailedDebugging - Internal use only  * **ShiftTranslationMillimetres** - distance projection will be shifted in mm.  * **ShiftRotationDegrees** - number of degrees projection will be rotated     Some of these parameters can be modified via API while the system is running. See &#x60;/UpdateServerConfiguration&#x60;.
        /// </remarks>
        /// <exception cref="VisionAndProjectionService.Swagger.Client.ApiException">Thrown when fails to make API call</exception>
        /// <returns>Task of ResultDtoServiceProjectionConfigurationDto</returns>
        System.Threading.Tasks.Task<ResultDtoServiceProjectionConfigurationDto> CoreLaserServiceGetProjectionConfigurationAsync ();

